[2026-03-16T00:09:07.720Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fz19pVsDs1LzasxtVReYRE","type":"tool_result","content":"    80→    80→`RECORD_REPLAY_API_KEY` must be set in the environment. It is already available in this\n    81→    81→container. The Playwright config passes it to the reporter via:\n    82→    82→\n    83→    83→```ts\n    84→    84→apiKey: process.env.REPLAY_API_KEY ?? process.env.RECORD_REPLAY_API_KEY\n    85→    85→```\n    86→    86→\n    87→    87→### 4. Playwright config\n    88→    88→\n    89→    89→The Playwright config MUST:\n    90→    90→\n    91→    91→1. Import BOTH `replayReporter` and `devices as replayDevices` from `@replayio/playwright`.\n    92→    92→2. Include `replayReporter(...)` in the `reporter` array with `upload: false`. Uploads are\n    93→    93→   handled by the test script, NOT by the reporter.\n    94→    94→3. Spread `replayDevices['Replay Chromium']` into the global `use` config. This sets\n    95→    95→   `executablePath`, `RECORD_ALL_CONTENT`, and critically `RECORD_REPLAY_METADATA_FILE` which\n    96→    96→   is required for the reporter to attach test metadata (pass/fail result) to recordings.\n    97→    97→   Without `RECORD_REPLAY_METADATA_FILE`, the recording driver cannot read the per-test\n    98→    98→   metadata written by the fixture, and all recordings will have empty `testResult`.\n    99→    99→\n   100→   100→**IMPORTANT**: Do NOT manually set `launchOptions.executablePath` and `env` instead of using\n   101→   101→`replayDevices['Replay Chromium']`. Manual config misses `RECORD_REPLAY_METADATA_FILE`,\n   102→   102→which breaks the recording-to-test metadata association.\n   103→   103→\n   104→   104→**IMPORTANT**: The Replay Chromium browser adds instrumentation overhead that makes all\n   105→   105→operations ~2–3x slower than standard Chromium. Always set higher timeouts from the start:\n   106→   106→\n   107→   107→- `actionTimeout: 15000` (15s for clicks, fills, etc.)\n   108→   108→- `navigationTimeout: 30000` (30s for page navigations)\n   109→   109→- Use `expect.toBeVisible({ timeout: 10000 })` for post-navigation assertions\n   110→   110→\n   111→   111→Example:\n   112→   112→\n   113→   113→```ts\n   114→   114→import { defineConfig, devices } from '@playwright/test';\n   115→   115→import { devices as replayDevices, replayReporter } from '@replayio/playwright';\n   116→   116→\n   117→   117→export default defineConfig({\n   118→   118→  // Replay Chromium is slower due to instrumentation — use generous timeouts\n   119→   119→  actionTimeout: 15000,\n   120→   120→  navigationTimeout: 30000,\n   121→   121→  reporter: [\n   122→   122→    replayReporter({\n   123→   123→      apiKey: process.env.REPLAY_API_KEY ?? process.env.RECORD_REPLAY_API_KEY,\n   124→   124→      upload: false,\n   125→   125→    }),\n   126→   126→    ['json', { outputFile: 'test-results/results.json' }],\n   127→   127→    ['list'],\n   128→   128→  ],\n   129→   129→  use: {\n   130→   130→    ...replayDevices['Replay Chromium'],\n   131→   131→  },\n   132→   132→});\n   133→   133→```\n   134→   134→\n   135→   135→### 5. Replay CLI commands reference\n   136→   136→\n   137→   137→- `npx replayio list` — List all local recordings (ID, host, date, duration, status).\n   138→   138→- `npx replayio list --json` — Full JSON metadata for all recordings. Each entry includes:\n   139→   139→  `id`, `buildId`, `date`, `duration`, `metadata` (host, URI, sourceMaps, processType),\n   140→   140→  `path`, `recordingStatus` (one of `\"recording\"`, `\"finished\"`, `\"crashed\"`).\n   141→   141→- `npx replayio upload <id>` — Upload a single recording by ID. Returns the viewable URL.\n   142→   142→- `npx replayio upload --all` — Upload all local recordings.\n   143→   143→- `npx replayio remove --all` — Delete all local recordings (use between runs to avoid stale\n   144→   144→  data accumulating).\n   145→   145→\n   146→   146→### 6. OpenSSL 1.1 requirement\n   147→   147→\n   148→   148→The Replay browser's recording driver requires `libcrypto.so.1.1` (OpenSSL 1.1). If the\n   149→   149→container only has OpenSSL 3, the browser will run but silently fail to record (no error in\n   150→   150→test output, just `DoLoadDriverHandle: dlopen failed` in stderr). Fix: download Ubuntu 18.04's\n   151→   151→`libssl1.1` deb, extract it, and set `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` to point at the extracted libs. See\n   152→   152→the deployment Playwright config for a working example.\n   153→   153→\n   154→   154→### 7. Pre-test verification\n   155→   155→\n   156→   156→Before running tests for the first time in an app, verify the Replay browser is installed:\n   157→   157→\n   158→   158→```bash\n   159→   159→ls ~/.replay/runtimes/chrome-linux/chrome"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"febec6c6-a46f-4d38-bc02-36d34589061b","uuid":"2a7467a8-2b45-4f02-a321-042741429724","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/agent/.claude/projects/-repo/febec6c6-a46f-4d38-bc02-36d34589061b/tool-results/toolu_01MVa1bPz8fHdBncAmkg4ijz.txt","content":"    80→`RECORD_REPLAY_API_KEY` must be set in the environment. It is already available in this\n    81→container. The Playwright config passes it to the reporter via:\n    82→\n    83→```ts\n    84→apiKey: process.env.REPLAY_API_KEY ?? process.env.RECORD_REPLAY_API_KEY\n    85→```\n    86→\n    87→### 4. Playwright config\n    88→\n    89→The Playwright config MUST:\n    90→\n    91→1. Import BOTH `replayReporter` and `devices as replayDevices` from `@replayio/playwright`.\n    92→2. Include `replayReporter(...)` in the `reporter` array with `upload: false`. Uploads are\n    93→   handled by the test script, NOT by the reporter.\n    94→3. Spread `replayDevices['Replay Chromium']` into the global `use` config. This sets\n    95→   `executablePath`, `RECORD_ALL_CONTENT`, and critically `RECORD_REPLAY_METADATA_FILE` which\n    96→   is required for the reporter to attach test metadata (pass/fail result) to recordings.\n    97→   Without `RECORD_REPLAY_METADATA_FILE`, the recording driver cannot read the per-test\n    98→   metadata written by the fixture, and all recordings will have empty `testResult`.\n    99→\n   100→**IMPORTANT**: Do NOT manually set `launchOptions.executablePath` and `env` instead of using\n   101→`replayDevices['Replay Chromium']`. Manual config misses `RECORD_REPLAY_METADATA_FILE`,\n   102→which breaks the recording-to-test metadata association.\n   103→\n   104→**IMPORTANT**: The Replay Chromium browser adds instrumentation overhead that makes all\n   105→operations ~2–3x slower than standard Chromium. Always set higher timeouts from the start:\n   106→\n   107→- `actionTimeout: 15000` (15s for clicks, fills, etc.)\n   108→- `navigationTimeout: 30000` (30s for page navigations)\n   109→- Use `expect.toBeVisible({ timeout: 10000 })` for post-navigation assertions\n   110→\n   111→Example:\n   112→\n   113→```ts\n   114→import { defineConfig, devices } from '@playwright/test';\n   115→import { devices as replayDevices, replayReporter } from '@replayio/playwright';\n   116→\n   117→export default defineConfig({\n   118→  // Replay Chromium is slower due to instrumentation — use generous timeouts\n   119→  actionTimeout: 15000,\n   120→  navigationTimeout: 30000,\n   121→  reporter: [\n   122→    replayReporter({\n   123→      apiKey: process.env.REPLAY_API_KEY ?? process.env.RECORD_REPLAY_API_KEY,\n   124→      upload: false,\n   125→    }),\n   126→    ['json', { outputFile: 'test-results/results.json' }],\n   127→    ['list'],\n   128→  ],\n   129→  use: {\n   130→    ...replayDevices['Replay Chromium'],\n   131→  },\n   132→});\n   133→```\n   134→\n   135→### 5. Replay CLI commands reference\n   136→\n   137→- `npx replayio list` — List all local recordings (ID, host, date, duration, status).\n   138→- `npx replayio list --json` — Full JSON metadata for all recordings. Each entry includes:\n   139→  `id`, `buildId`, `date`, `duration`, `metadata` (host, URI, sourceMaps, processType),\n   140→  `path`, `recordingStatus` (one of `\"recording\"`, `\"finished\"`, `\"crashed\"`).\n   141→- `npx replayio upload <id>` — Upload a single recording by ID. Returns the viewable URL.\n   142→- `npx replayio upload --all` — Upload all local recordings.\n   143→- `npx replayio remove --all` — Delete all local recordings (use between runs to avoid stale\n   144→  data accumulating).\n   145→\n   146→### 6. OpenSSL 1.1 requirement\n   147→\n   148→The Replay browser's recording driver requires `libcrypto.so.1.1` (OpenSSL 1.1). If the\n   149→container only has OpenSSL 3, the browser will run but silently fail to record (no error in\n   150→test output, just `DoLoadDriverHandle: dlopen failed` in stderr). Fix: download Ubuntu 18.04's\n   151→`libssl1.1` deb, extract it, and set `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` to point at the extracted libs. See\n   152→the deployment Playwright config for a working example.\n   153→\n   154→### 7. Pre-test verification\n   155→\n   156→Before running tests for the first time in an app, verify the Replay browser is installed:\n   157→\n   158→```bash\n   159→ls ~/.replay/runtimes/chrome-linux/chrome","numLines":80,"startLine":80,"totalLines":944}}}
