[2026-03-16T00:09:11.410Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MRfFVVnA2uovZ4LtKvNXzN","type":"tool_result","content":"   158→   158→```bash\n   159→   159→ls ~/.replay/runtimes/chrome-linux/chrome\n   160→   160→```\n   161→   161→\n   162→   162→If it does not exist, run `npx replayio install` before any test execution. Running tests\n   163→   163→without the Replay browser means failures produce no recordings, making debugging impossible.\n   164→   164→Do not defer Replay installation to after failures are discovered.\n   165→   165→\n   166→   166→## Pre-Flight Checks\n   167→   167→\n   168→   168→Before running any tests, run the standard pre-flight procedure from `skills/scripts/preflight.md`.\n   169→   169→Run each preflight step as a **separate command** — do NOT chain them with `&&` or `;` in a\n   170→   170→single command. Chained commands fail if any sub-command fails (especially `pkill` when no\n   171→   171→process exists), producing confusing output and wasting effort decomposing and re-running.\n   172→   172→\n   173→   173→```bash\n   174→   174→# Step 1: Kill stale servers (including zombies holding port 8888)\n   175→   175→pkill -f \"netlify|vite\" 2>/dev/null || true\n   176→   176→# If port 8888 is still occupied after pkill (zombie processes invisible to lsof),\n   177→   177→# find PIDs via /proc/net/tcp6 and kill -9 them:\n   178→   178→fuser -k 8888/tcp 2>/dev/null || true\n   179→   179→```\n   180→   180→```bash\n   181→   181→# Step 2: Verify env vars\n   182→   182→grep NEON_PROJECT_ID .env || echo \"ERROR: NEON_PROJECT_ID not set\"\n   183→   183→```\n   184→   184→```bash\n   185→   185→# Step 3: Verify Replay browser\n   186→   186→ls ~/.replay/runtimes/chrome-linux/chrome 2>/dev/null || npx replayio install\n   187→   187→```\n   188→   188→```bash\n   189→   189→# Step 4: Verify dependencies\n   190→   190→ls node_modules/@neondatabase/serverless 2>/dev/null || npm install --legacy-peer-deps\n   191→   191→```\n   192→   192→```bash\n   193→   193→# Step 5: Clear stale recordings\n   194→   194→npx replayio remove --all 2>/dev/null\n   195→   195→```\n   196→   196→\n   197→   197→See `skills/scripts/preflight.md` for the full pre-flight checklist and\n   198→   198→`skills/scripts/env-setup.md` for environment prerequisites.\n   199→   199→\n   200→   200→## Running Tests\n   201→   201→\n   202→   202→Run tests via `npm run test <testFile>` from the app directory (see `skills/scripts/test.md`\n   203→   203→for the full script specification). Do NOT manually run playwright or start dev servers.\n   204→   204→\n   205→   205→ULTRA IMPORTANT: NEVER EVER EVER RUN `npx playwright test`. You must use the provided test script.\n   206→   206→\n   207→   207→- The script prints a one-line summary to stdout (e.g., `8 passed, 2 failed — see logs/test-run-3.log`).\n   208→   208→- Full test output and recording metadata are in the log file referenced by the summary.\n   209→   209→- Read the log file only when you need to diagnose failures.\n   210→   210→- Tests MUST run in parallel with multiple workers (use `fullyParallel: true` in playwright config).\n   211→   211→\n   212→   212→**ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED on first run**: If the first test run fails with\n   213→   213→`ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED`, the dev server likely wasn't fully ready. Wait 5 seconds and retry\n   214→   214→once before investigating further. Do not immediately launch into manual `netlify dev` startup\n   215→   215→or port debugging — the test script manages the server automatically and a single retry usually\n   216→   216→resolves transient startup delays.\n   217→   217→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"febec6c6-a46f-4d38-bc02-36d34589061b","uuid":"f260849a-df80-496a-b737-c876ad147e9c","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/agent/.claude/projects/-repo/febec6c6-a46f-4d38-bc02-36d34589061b/tool-results/toolu_01MVa1bPz8fHdBncAmkg4ijz.txt","content":"   158→```bash\n   159→ls ~/.replay/runtimes/chrome-linux/chrome\n   160→```\n   161→\n   162→If it does not exist, run `npx replayio install` before any test execution. Running tests\n   163→without the Replay browser means failures produce no recordings, making debugging impossible.\n   164→Do not defer Replay installation to after failures are discovered.\n   165→\n   166→## Pre-Flight Checks\n   167→\n   168→Before running any tests, run the standard pre-flight procedure from `skills/scripts/preflight.md`.\n   169→Run each preflight step as a **separate command** — do NOT chain them with `&&` or `;` in a\n   170→single command. Chained commands fail if any sub-command fails (especially `pkill` when no\n   171→process exists), producing confusing output and wasting effort decomposing and re-running.\n   172→\n   173→```bash\n   174→# Step 1: Kill stale servers (including zombies holding port 8888)\n   175→pkill -f \"netlify|vite\" 2>/dev/null || true\n   176→# If port 8888 is still occupied after pkill (zombie processes invisible to lsof),\n   177→# find PIDs via /proc/net/tcp6 and kill -9 them:\n   178→fuser -k 8888/tcp 2>/dev/null || true\n   179→```\n   180→```bash\n   181→# Step 2: Verify env vars\n   182→grep NEON_PROJECT_ID .env || echo \"ERROR: NEON_PROJECT_ID not set\"\n   183→```\n   184→```bash\n   185→# Step 3: Verify Replay browser\n   186→ls ~/.replay/runtimes/chrome-linux/chrome 2>/dev/null || npx replayio install\n   187→```\n   188→```bash\n   189→# Step 4: Verify dependencies\n   190→ls node_modules/@neondatabase/serverless 2>/dev/null || npm install --legacy-peer-deps\n   191→```\n   192→```bash\n   193→# Step 5: Clear stale recordings\n   194→npx replayio remove --all 2>/dev/null\n   195→```\n   196→\n   197→See `skills/scripts/preflight.md` for the full pre-flight checklist and\n   198→`skills/scripts/env-setup.md` for environment prerequisites.\n   199→\n   200→## Running Tests\n   201→\n   202→Run tests via `npm run test <testFile>` from the app directory (see `skills/scripts/test.md`\n   203→for the full script specification). Do NOT manually run playwright or start dev servers.\n   204→\n   205→ULTRA IMPORTANT: NEVER EVER EVER RUN `npx playwright test`. You must use the provided test script.\n   206→\n   207→- The script prints a one-line summary to stdout (e.g., `8 passed, 2 failed — see logs/test-run-3.log`).\n   208→- Full test output and recording metadata are in the log file referenced by the summary.\n   209→- Read the log file only when you need to diagnose failures.\n   210→- Tests MUST run in parallel with multiple workers (use `fullyParallel: true` in playwright config).\n   211→\n   212→**ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED on first run**: If the first test run fails with\n   213→`ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED`, the dev server likely wasn't fully ready. Wait 5 seconds and retry\n   214→once before investigating further. Do not immediately launch into manual `netlify dev` startup\n   215→or port debugging — the test script manages the server automatically and a single retry usually\n   216→resolves transient startup delays.\n   217→","numLines":60,"startLine":158,"totalLines":944}}}
